# ==============================================================================
# DG-NET  —  STAGE 1: Dis-Net  (Warp Field Estimator)
# DTD-FSRN dataset  |  Based on Thapa et al., ICCV 2021
#
# Architecture:
#   Three parallel CNN branches (one per input frame) each estimate a warp
#   map from a single distorted image.  The three maps are fed as a temporal
#   sequence into two stacked ConvLSTM layers which enforce temporal
#   consistency.  The final refined map is the prediction for the middle frame.
#
# Physics losses (Thapa et al. §3.1):
#   L_W  — scale-invariant error vs GT warp map    (three components)
#   L_R  — refraction consistency:  re-distort the input with predicted warp,
#           compare to original.  Self-supervised — does NOT need GT warp.
#   L_C  — temporal consistency: un-warp each of the 3 frames and compare
#           pairwise.  All three frames should reveal the same scene.
#
# Why this fixes the flat-field collapse:
#   L_R provides a gradient even when GT supervision is weak: if the network
#   predicts zero displacement, re-applying zero warp leaves the distorted
#   image unchanged — and that is NOT consistent with the GT height map used
#   to generate the distortion, so L_R penalises it strongly.
#
# Multi-session resumable:
#   Full state (model, optimiser, scaler, RNG, loss history) is checkpointed
#   atomically after every epoch.  Set EPOCHS_PER_RUN and re-run the cell
#   to continue from where the previous Kaggle session left off.
#
# Output:
#   /kaggle/working/dgnet_stage1/checkpoints/resume_state.pth
#   /kaggle/working/dgnet_stage1/checkpoints/disnet_epoch{N}.pth
#   /kaggle/working/dgnet_stage1/checkpoints/disnet_final.pth   (when done)
#   /kaggle/working/dgnet_stage1/epoch_loss_log.csv
#   /kaggle/working/dgnet_stage1/warp_stats.json
#   /kaggle/working/dgnet_stage1/samples/epoch_{N:03d}.png
# ==============================================================================

